xnu 0497: boot the adsp through PAS1

Add bsd/dev/mondrian_adsp.c: an opt-in worker (mondrianadsp=1) that reads
the joined /private/var/vm/adsp.mbn (tools/adsp-image.py), maps the
0x9fd00000 carve-out and the APPS-ADSP SMEM/IPCC/mutex windows in
mondrian_log_start premap, hands the ELF header and hash segment to PAS1
init_image, sets up the relocatable span, copies the loadable segments,
calls auth_and_reset and polls the ADSP slave-kernel SMP2P entry for the
ready bit. It initializes the host outbound SMP2P item and rings the
LPASS SMP2P doorbell before the load. No QMP load-state vote, RPMh rail
vote, GLINK or GPR yet: those are the next milestones if PAS alone does
not bring the ADSP up.

